From 14be813407db5952112bbe2bb7823b37369f6619 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anirudh Acharya <anirudhra@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:28:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: ifc6410: add GPU vddcx regulator supply

Add IFC6410 board-level vddcx supply reference for the Adreno 320 GPU.
Use PM8921 S3 as the GPU vddcx supply, matching the historical APQ8064
DTS usage for the Adreno CX rail. Do not add a GPU vdd supply or OPP
voltage corners here because the IFC6410 GPU core rail and voltage
corners have not been validated.

Signed-off-by: Anirudh Acharya <anirudhra@hotmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-ifc6410.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-ifc6410.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-ifc6410.dts
index 30daca665418..4dd2d1dd2541 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-ifc6410.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-ifc6410.dts
@@ -329,6 +329,10 @@ lvs6 {
 	};
 };
 
+&gpu {
+	vddcx-supply = <&pm8921_s3>;
+};
+
 &sata_phy0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
2.48.1
